flowchart TB
    accTitle: How Renovate runs for each repository
    accDescr: In the blueprint, a job with a token that only reads lists the repositories of the release app that may have rules for Renovate. Renovate then runs once for each of them, two at a time, each run with a token for its one repository, which the run looks at before Renovate starts. A last job, without the private key of the app, brings the log of every run into the one issue of Renovate's problems.

    list["`**repositories of Renovate**<br>a token that only reads<br>lists the repositories of the release app`"]
    first["`**renovate app**<br>a token for app alone,<br>looked at before Renovate starts`"]
    second["`**renovate other**<br>a token for other alone,<br>looked at before Renovate starts`"]
    report["`**problems of Renovate**<br>no private key: the log of every run<br>in the one issue of its problems`"]
    updates["Pull requests with the updates,<br>in each repository"]

    list -->|"two at a time"| first & second
    first & second --> report
    first & second --> updates

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class list,first,second,report bot
    class updates done
